+<div style="font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FC5305;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:8px">Dispatch update</div>
+<h1 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:25px;line-height:1.28;color:#0f172a;font-weight:800">Your dispatcher can only sell a truck they can see.</h1>
+
+<p style="margin:0 0 14px">When we don&rsquo;t know where your truck is this morning &mdash; or where it delivers and when it frees up &mdash; we are guessing. Guessing loses loads to the carrier who told their dispatcher first.</p>
+
+<p style="margin:0 0 18px">So starting today, your dedicated LoadBoot dispatcher works your loads <strong>only while your truck&rsquo;s availability is posted and confirmed in the app within the last 24 hours.</strong> No fresh post, no sourcing. Same rule the best fleets already run internally.</p>
